# Thousand-Year Storm: "copy it for each other instant and sorcery spell you've cast before it this turn." A countered spell was
# still cast (CR 601.2i), a spell cast on another turn is not "this turn", and an opponent's spell is not one "you've cast".
# Bot1 pays for Storm on turn 1 and casts a Lightning Bolt on turn 3 (not copied: the first this turn). On turn 5 Bot1 casts
# Bolt B, which Bot2 counters with Counterspell (Bot2's own spell counts for nothing), and then Bolt C: it is copied exactly once
# - for Bolt B, countered as it was, and not for the turn 3 Bolt: Bot2 takes 3 (turn 3) + 3 + 3 (turn 5) = 9.

